  "axis": [
    "Trend charts' y axis is roughly logarithmic: ticks are not evenly spaced in value but evenly spaced per decade (about 216 px per decade for vessels, about 137 for albicans, about 165 for follicle, about 155 for macrophage). Counts 0 and 1 sit in compressed rows at the bottom (0 is a separate row below 1 or 2, like a pseudo-log). x axis is age 20 to 70 and linear.",
    "Trends chart's y axis is logarithmic (about log10) for counts of 1 and above, with ticks such as 2, 5, 10, 20, 50, 100, 200, 500, 1000, 2000. The 0 tick sits about half a log step below 1, so zeros are plotted at about 0.5. Read values with 10^(interpolated log position). The x axis is age 20 to 70, linear. The comparison charts use linear axes."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "All values are eyeballed interpolations. Vessel lines are straight on the log scale (rf about -3.6e-3 log10 per year, seg about -6e-3). Follicle lines curve down and end steeply near age 58.6 (rf) and 59 (seg); the lines ending reflect a log-transform fit, so ages 60 and up are null. Macrophage seg line stays above 0 but falls to about 2 at 70. Albicans seg line is a mild rise from 16 to 39. Percentile bands are rough, especially in the sparse 30s (few donors) and where dots overlap; the zero share is estimated from the visible 0-row dots (lighter dots may hide overlap). Comparison panels: vessel, albicans and follicle crops contain parts of neighboring panels, only the titled panel was read; the cmp axes were read from tick pixel spacing, so maxima are approximate (the macrophage y max is about 350, the top tick).",
    "All numbers are visual estimates from pixel positions, good to about 10 to 20 percent. The follicle lines curve down steeply and end at about age 58.5 for rf and 59 for seg, so those lines are null from age 60. Band values and zero shares are rough, because overlapping dots hide each other and zeros of one method can sit under the other's dots. The macrophage seg line is still about 2 at age 70, so zeroAge is null. The albicans rf line and seg line are reported as smooth curves read at a few pixel positions. Vessel y axis has no 0 tick. Seg zero shares for macrophage are from counting the zero row of dots; rf has none at 0.",
    "Third reading (resolving the disagreements): tick rows and the lines measured to the pixel on the crops (follicle: 165 px per decade, 0 at log10 0.5; macrophage: 156 px per decade; albicans: 137 px per decade); bands as the 10th, 50th and 90th percentiles of the dots of each decade, counted by eye on 2x enlargements. Zeros of one method hide under the other's dots, so zero shares stay rough. The trend lines read as straight lines in raw counts drawn on the log axis (the follicle lines reach 0 at about 58.5 and 59, the macrophage Seg line at about 72), so they are interpolated linearly in counts."
  ],
